#{[17592186401586 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186473778 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186401586 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186473779 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186401586 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186473780 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186401586 #edb/ref 1069 "q-168921" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401586 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401586 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ and the ellipse $4{x}^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=1?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is a type I region\n- **II.** It is a type II region\n- **III.** It's neither a type I nor a type II region" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186401586 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fd6f7437-bc45-50cb-9400-bcd422c5b408" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186401586 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/bc/bc6b71d1fe69abd34dbd939dc62ede5201b75713e25456cf084e889bc44f449e.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=0.4$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](images/4a/4a1fd7069abaa3b3fa4d9c286773d226798bf3ad565e85663cab44557fd635c1.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=-1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](images/26/260e8e959ca95a029a98bd4102106a66df418ea73c0640398c8fdebfdbf812f6.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406975 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406975 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406975 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406985 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406975 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406975 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406987 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406975 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406975 #edb/ref 1045 "Type I and II Regions in Two-Dimensional Space" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406975 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186406984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406975 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406975 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050822 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406975 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "3da669c9-a862-59b7-84e5-f7ce7ac62942" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406982 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186474034 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186406982 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186474035 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186406982 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186474036 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186406982 #edb/ref 1069 "q-72160" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406982 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406982 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the curves $y={x}^{3}$ and $y=\\sqrt[3]{x},$ in the first quadrant?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** It is a type I region\n- **II.** It is a type II region\n- **III.** It's neither a type I nor a type II region" #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186406982 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0d779a1b-dcae-59f0-822c-7860f9483ab7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406982 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y={x}^{3}\\, & ⟹\\,x=\\sqrt[3]{y} \\\\ y=\\sqrt[3]{x}\\, & ⟹\\,x={y}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/89/899357795c6d5b81d3cb619d71493ad787645697fe1f2fcecda78c1b875f388e.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,{x}^{3}\\le y\\le \\sqrt[3]{x}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,{y}^{3}\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{y}}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406983 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186406985 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406983 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0868f274-6d6e-5256-97a9-564c4f1a8169" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406983 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186393194 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406984 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186406983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406984 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "11bc950f-28ab-5ada-8524-78d17fbdb0fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406984 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186339049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406985 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186406987 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406985 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1c227960-e1d3-5f07-b75a-31b153d00a8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406985 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186373174 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406986 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "52cd1fa6-d29c-562d-9d88-cade3cec5a66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406986 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186339070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406987 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186406986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406987 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fd242e61-69b5-5bfd-bc83-d7379d3f45c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406987 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186406982 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186408166 #edb/ref 10 :answer-field.type/checkbox #edb/ref 17592186045416] [17592186429961 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186429976 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429961 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186429977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429961 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186429978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429961 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186429979 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429961 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186429980 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429961 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429961 #edb/ref 1045 "Type I and II Regions in Two-Dimensional Space" #edb/ref 1759218604